<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F6.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S6.F6.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">D1T3</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="S6.F6.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.09482v1/rel-trial-study-outcome-column-permutation_independent-sds_vs_k.svg" id="S6.F6.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/284;" width="476" height="284"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F6.sf4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(d)</span> </span><span id="S6.F6.sf4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">D6T1</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="S6.F6.sf5" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.09482v1/rel-trial-study-adverse-column-permutation_independent-sds_vs_k.svg" id="S6.F6.sf5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/299;" width="476" height="299"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F6.sf5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(e)</span> </span><span id="S6.F6.sf5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">D6T2</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="S6.F6.sf6" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.09482v1/rel-trial-site-success-column-permutation_independent-sds_vs_k.svg" id="S6.F6.sf6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/292;" width="476" height="292"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F6.sf6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(f)</span> </span><span id="S6.F6.sf6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">D6T3</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S6.F6.sf7" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.09482v1/rel-hm-user-churn-column-permutation_independent-sds_vs_k.svg" id="S6.F6.sf7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/276;" width="476" height="276"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F6.sf7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(g)</span> </span><span id="S6.F6.sf7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">D4T1</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S6.F6.sf8" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.09482v1/rel-hm-item-sales-column-permutation_independent-sds_vs_k.svg" id="S6.F6.sf8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/284;" width="476" height="284"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F6.sf8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(h)</span> </span><span id="S6.F6.sf8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">D4T2</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>. </span><span id="S6.F6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Soft determinacy versus conciseness for <span id="S6.F6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">Projection</span> explanations, for <math id="S6.F6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> tasks and database perturbation <math id="S6.F6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\mathsf{ind}}_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>𝗂𝗇𝖽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\mathsf{ind}}_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2. </span><span id="S6.SS2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">FKJoin</span> Evaluation</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S6.F7" title="In 6.2. FKJoin Evaluation ‣ 6. Experimental Evaluation ‣ Database Views as Explanations for Relational Deep Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows the corresponding set of results for <span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">FKJoin</span>.
As in <span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">Projection</span>, the mask-based approach <span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FKPK Mask</span> is significantly faster than the greedy baseline <span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Greedy Expansion</span>. In terms of deviation from determinacy, the gap between <span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FKPK Mask</span> and <span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Greedy Expansion</span> is smaller, but <span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FKPK Mask</span> still edges out on average.
The differences between the two perturbations strategies are again minor, verifying the robustness of our metric.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S6.F7.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.09482v1/time_comparison_legend_fkpk.svg" id="S6.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/45;" width="476" height="45"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S6.F7.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.09482v1/dev_from_determinacy_combined_fkpk_foreign_key_uniform_random.png" id="S6.F7.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/58;" width="381" height="58" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F7.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S6.F7.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Deviation from determinacy <math id="S6.F7.sf1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dev}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖽𝖾𝗏</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dev}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> for each database-task and database perturbation <math id="S6.F7.sf1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\mathsf{uniform}}_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>𝗎𝗇𝗂𝖿𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\mathsf{uniform}}_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S6.F7.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.09482v1/dev_from_determinacy_combined_fkpk_foreign_key_hist_random.png" id="S6.F7.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/58;" width="381" height="58" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F7.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S6.F7.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Deviation from determinacy <math id="S6.F7.sf2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dev}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖽𝖾𝗏</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dev}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> for each database-task and database perturbation <math id="S6.F7.sf2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\mathsf{freq}}_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>𝖿𝗋𝖾𝗊</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\mathsf{freq}}_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S6.F7.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.09482v1/time_comparison_fkpk_foreign_key_uniform_random.svg" id="S6.F7.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/60;" width="381" height="60"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F7.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S6.F7.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Time to obtain explanation for each database-task and <math id="S6.F7.sf3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\mathsf{uniform}}_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>𝗎𝗇𝗂𝖿𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\mathsf{uniform}}_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>. Results for <math id="S6.F7.sf3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\mathsf{freq}}_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>𝖿𝗋𝖾𝗊</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\mathsf{freq}}_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> are similar.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>. </span><span id="S6.F7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Evaluation for <span id="S6.F7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">FKJoin</span>. For visualization purposes, tasks are separated into “easy” (left) and “hard” (right) ones, with separate <math id="S6.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{dev}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖽𝖾𝗏</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{dev}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> scales. The average (AVG) across all tasks is also shown. Below the dataset and task name, we indicate the explanation size <math id="S6.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and the total number of foreign-key constraints.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3. </span>Case Study</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perform a case study on the rel-trial dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Initiative et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, a large-scale relational dataset from clinical trial reports.
It contains 15 tables with a total of 5,852,157 rows and 140 attributes, out of which 110 are data attributes and 30 are key or foreign-key attributes.
We focus on the study-outcome task (D6T1), a binary classification task that predicts whether a trial achieves its primary outcome.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>. </span><span id="S6.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Case study (<a href="#S6.SS3" title="6.3. Case Study ‣ 6. Experimental Evaluation ‣ Database Views as Explanations for Relational Deep Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a>): Explanation Metrics by Explanation Language for D6T1.
</span></figcaption>
